# services/rules-service/.env.example
#
# Copy to `services/rules-service/.env` — the service loads this path
# independently of the directory from which start.sh or uvicorn is invoked.
# Every variable below corresponds to a field in app.config.Settings.
# Defaults shown are what app/config.Settings applies when the env var is unset.

# --- Database ---
# Lift provenance: DATABASE_URL is the connection string used by app/database.py:create_engine.
#
# Phase-F2 update: TWO supported modes --
#
# (A) Developer-laptop dev (DEFAULT): SQLite relative path. Both
#     rules-service and Finlynq (Phase-F2a shared DB) resolve to
#     ``<project_root>/finance.db`` when each uvicorn is launched from
#     the project root via ``start.sh``. start.sh ensures CWD is the
#     project root before the children inherit DATABASE_URL. DO NOT
#     launch from inside services/rules-service/ or services/finlynq/
#     with this default -- the SQLite path resolves relative to CWD and
#     would diverge.
#
# (B) Postgres-integration (CI / docker-compose): the sidecar at
#     localhost:5432 -- start docker-compose up db to bring it up.
#     TEST_DATABASE_URL (only honored by services/rules-service/tests/conftest.py)
#     points at the dedicated test DB (``wealthiq_routes_test``).
#
# Choose ONE. Postgres-sidecar mode is for integration testing ONLY;
# SQLite is the canonical dev path going forward (single-file DB is
# trivially hermetic + versioning-friendly via /data file backups).
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./finance.db
# TEST_DATABASE_URL is read by tests/conftest.py ONLY (not by app.config).
# Set to ``postgresql+psycopg2://postgres@localhost:5432/wealthiq_routes_test``
# for a CI run with the sidecar up; leave blank for default SQLite-memory.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# --- Application ---
ENVIRONMENT=development
APP_NAME=Finance Copilot
APP_VERSION=0.1.0
# Single-user auth (§10 decision 4). Default `alex`. JWTs issued for other values will be rejected.
LOCAL_USER=alex

# --- Security ---
# IMPORTANT: override in any non-dev environment. HS256 + a known weak/dev default is fine locally.
JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-change-in-production
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
# Token TTL in hours; cookie Max-Age is 3600 * this.
JWT_EXPIRATION_HOURS=24

# --- API server (Docker / uvicorn entry point) ---
API_HOST=0.0.0.0
API_PORT=8000

# --- Plaid (canonical ingest path per §10 decision 1; required if you call Plaid endpoints) ---
PLAID_CLIENT_ID=
PLAID_SECRET=
PLAID_ENV=sandbox

# --- Finnhub analyst ratings (Phase 9, free-tier) ---
# Drives the GET /api/analyst-ratings/{ticker} endpoint that powers the
# "Analyst Insights" panel on /recommendations.
#   • Get a free key (no credit card, 60 calls/min, US/global coverage):
#       1. Visit https://finnhub.io/register
#       2. Confirm email; the dashboard shows your API key.
#       3. Paste it below and restart the rules-service.
#   • Without a key the endpoint returns HTTP 500 with detail
#     "Analyst ratings service is not configured (missing API key)." so
#     the bad config is loud, not silent.
#   • Upstream rate-limit / rejected-key errors surface as HTTP 502 so
#     the FE renders a retry banner instead of "no consensus".
#   • 24h response cache (TTLCache) caps the upstream call rate well
#     within the 60/min free tier for single-user local-dev.
#   ★ Leave the line EMPTY (default below) until you have a real key.
#     A non-empty placeholder like 'changeme' would skip the
#     helpful 500 branch (the route's 'if not api_key' short-circuits
#     on empty-string only) and ship the bogus token straight to
#     Finnhub, which 401s and surfaces an opaque 502.
FINNHUB_API_KEY=
#   ★ Docker compose note: this file is consumed by 'start.sh' via
#     uvicorn inheriting the host env. The docker-compose.yml at the
#     project root does NOT bind env_file. Operators on the Docker path
#     need EITHER:
#       (a) env_file: ./services/rules-service/.env under the
#           rules-service service, OR
#       (b) environment: { FINNHUB_API_KEY: ${FINNHUB_API_KEY} } to
#           compose from the host shell.
#     Without one of those, 'docker-compose up' silently hits the
#     missing-key 500 even after you've pasted the key below.

# --- Finlynq canonical store (Phase F4) ---
# rules-service's /api/categories/{/*}, /api/dashboard/summary, and
# /api/imports/upload routes are thin httpx forwarders to Finlynq.
# This URL is what they POST/GET/PUT against.
#   • Match services/finlynq/.env.example's API_PORT (default 8001).
#   • Inside Docker compose, rules-service cannot resolve
#     ``localhost`` to the host — use the SERVICE name instead:
#       FINLYNQ_BASE_URL=http://finlynq:8001
#   • In start.sh (dev), the host-resolved default 'http://localhost:8001'
#     works because Finlynq boots on the same machine.
#   • If Finlynq is unreachable, the forwarders surface HTTP 502
#     with ``{"detail": "..."}``; the FE renders the retry banner instead
#     of a misleading 500.
FINLYNQ_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001

# --- Phase 1 forecast persistence gate (ADR-006) ---
# ATLAS_FORECAST_PERSISTENCE_ENABLED gates the trusted forecast
# generation service.  Default-off.
#
#   • Uncomment + set to ``true`` ONLY after bounded operator
#     validation has succeeded AND a retention / deletion policy has
#     been approved.
#   • Unparseable values (e.g. ``maybe``) cause Settings() to raise, so
#     the service fails closed at startup.
#   • Explicit ``true`` / ``1`` / ``yes`` / ``on`` enable persistence.
#   • Explicit ``false`` / ``0`` / ``no`` / ``off`` and an absent
#     variable keep persistence disabled (default).
#
# This file documents the flag as DISABLED. The checked-in example
# MUST stay disabled until Phase 1 exit criteria are approved.
# ATLAS_FORECAST_PERSISTENCE_ENABLED=false
